  "id": "COMPOUND:24902 - PROTEIN:5481",
  "verbalization": "Phyllofolactones F appears to be a multifaceted compound that exerts its biological effects through a series of interconnected pathways involving T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3. This protein is a key target for multiple compounds, including Traxillagenin, Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, and Caragasinin B, all of which ultimately lead to the target of interest, M059J. The evidence suggests that Phyllofolactones F may act as a common modulator of CD3, which in turn influences the activity of various downstream targets, including M059J. The consistent targeting of CD3 by different compounds implies a potential role for Phyllofolactones F in regulating CD3-dependent signaling pathways, possibly through a shared mechanism of action. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of CD3 as a central node in the biological network involving Phyllofolactones F and M059J.",
